{{Quote|So you need an alien who can channel energy? I think I know just the guy.|[[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] to [[Zak Saturday|Zak]], referring to Feedback.<ref name="TGIS">''[[T.G.I.S.]]''</ref>}}
Due to his body being negatively charged{{Refn|group = OV Brief|name = brief}} Feedback has a considerable amount of electricity at his disposal,{{Refn|Alternate versions of Feedback are shown generating electricity in different colors. For example, [[Weapon XI (Present)|17-year-old Mutant Kevin]]'s electricity is colored red.<ref>''[[Weapon XI: Part 2]]''</ref>|group = note}} and by extension he also has the power of electrokinesis, meaning that he can create and influence the direction and form of the electricity that's generated from his plug-like fingers and tail with extreme precision.<ref name="MM">''[[Max's Monster]]''</ref> This allows him to fire out beams of electrical energy,<ref name="TMTCP1>''[[The More Things Change: Part 1]]''</ref> charge up large bombs of electricity,<ref>''[[Let's Do the Time War Again]]''</ref> explosions of electricity<ref name="SD2" /> or something more complicated like waves of electricity.<ref name="VM">''[[Vreedlemania]]''</ref> Feedback's electricity is powerful enough to harm a [[Galvanic Mechamorph (Classic)|Galvanic Mechamorph]]<ref name="TH">''[[Trouble Helix]]''</ref> and an [[Ultimate Vaxasaurian]].<ref name="AFoB">''[[A Fistful of Brains]]''</ref> Additionally, Feedback can use his stored electricity to propel himself through the air at high speeds.<ref name="SD2" /> 

Feedback can conduct electricity throughout his body. Conductoids who inhabit the [[Teslavorr]] nebula use this ability to easily travel throughout it by using minute voltage differences between to propel themselves.{{Refn|group = OV Brief|name = brief}} Feedback has conducted electricity to enhance the power of his blows, as demonstrated in his first fight with [[Malware]],<ref name="TH" /> or increase his speed exponentially by running on electrical power lines.<ref name="SD1">''[[Showdown: Part 1]]''</ref>

Feedback's most notable ability is being able to absorb and redirect energy attacks, most commonly electricity, using his fingers, tendrils and tail.{{Refn|https://preservetube.com/watch?v&#61;CnTS1_7VAbE|group = CN}} He can use this ability physically or remotely on objects or opponents to drain them of their energy.<ref name="TMTCP1 /><ref>''[[A Jolt From the Past]]''</ref> Absorbing external energy will supercharge his electricity beams, making them more powerful. For instance, when Feedback plugged his tendrils and tail into the [[Helix]], absorbing it allowed him to fire out a massive beam of electricity, which effortlessly overpowered the blast from Malware's [[Tachyon Cannon]].<ref name="SD2" /> Feedback is able to absorb electricity generated by [[Nosedeenian (Classic)|Nosedeenian]]s and [[Terroranchula (Transformation)|Terroranchula]]s; an energy beam from a [[Tachyon Cannon]];<ref name='MF">''[[Malefactor]]''</ref> [[manna]];<ref name="TGIS" /> and a [[Crystalsapien (Classic)|Crystalsapien]]'s energy attacks.{{Refn|[[:File:Feedback Can Absorb Chromastone's Energy.png]]|group = DJW}} Additionally, Feedback can also redirect energy, as demonstrated when he redirected the [[Annihilarrgh]]'s energy at [[Maltruant]].<ref name="AND">''[[A New Dawn]]''</ref>

Feedback is able to stretch his tail and the tendrils on his head for more range.<ref name="MM"/> Using this ability, he can electrocute foes by directly "plugging" into them.<ref name="TH" /> These tendrils are also quite strong, enough to knock over [[Phil Billings (Classic)|Phil]] in his [[Terroranchula]] form.<ref name="WXIP1">[[Weapon XI: Part 1]]</ref> He can also use his tendrils to "smell" radio signals.<ref>''[[Clyde 5]]''</ref>

Feedback has enhanced strength, as he can lift Phil in his Terroranchula form<ref name="WXIP1" /> and charge into a building by busting down a wall with ease.<ref name="Breakpoint">''[[Breakpoint]]''</ref> Feedback also has enhanced durability, as he shrugged off a blast from a gigantic Malware<ref name="SD2" /> and was unfazed when Terroranchula Phil threw him against a wall.<ref name="MM" />

Feedback has enhanced jumping and is quite acrobatic. Feedback also has enhanced reflexes, being able to knock one of [[Ultimate Humungousaur]]'s missiles back at him.<ref name="AFoB" />

===Non-Canon Powers and Abilities===
====Galactic Champions====
Feedback has the ability to teleport in a flash of electricity.

====Ben 10: Omniverse (Video Game)====
Feedback can generate force-fields of electricity.

==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow">
MaxMonster44.png|Ineffective Electrokinesis
BP (274).png|Unstoppable Electricity Beams
</gallery>
Feedback's electric blasts are occasionally ineffective against opponents who can absorb electricity, such as Phil.<ref name="MM" />

Once Feedback powers up his electric energy blasts, he cannot stop himself from shooting them, meaning he will have to resort to shooting them all up in the air to avoid any collateral damage if he fails to catch his target.<ref name="Breakpoint" />

Feedback has an unknown limit to the amount of energy he can absorb.{{Refn|[[:File:Matt Wayne Feedback Absorption Limit.png]]|group = MW}}{{Refn|In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', following his reversion from [[Chromastone (Classic)|Chromastone]], [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] is depicted without a Celestialsapien arm formed by [[Skurd]]. This persists through the mass transformation sequence, which is also missing Skurd. After [[Feedback]] reverts back to Ben, he has a Celestialsapien arm (now on the opposite side), which a shot makes a point to show Skurd reverting. Due to the rushed production of Season 8 of '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''',{{Refn|[[:File:Rath Clothed Permanent 2.png]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:Skurd Development Details.png]]|group = DJW|name = production}} as well as the logistical cost of making new model sheets for aliens with a Celestialsapien arm and Skurd, it is assumed that both were present despite not being seen on-screen, and the Celestialsapien arm was likely a contributing factor towards Feedback's ability to contain and redirect the [[Annihilarrgh]]'s energy. Furthermore, when inquired about the shot, neither story editor [[Charlotte McDuffie]] or director [[Dan Riba]] recalled the intention.{{Refn|https://youtu.be/unaX1hKhOy4|group = CM}}|group = note}}

If Feedback is in the same vicinity as multiple other male Conductoids for too long, the identical polarity of their bodies could generate a potentially lethal arc through them.{{Refn|group = OV Brief|name = brief}}

===Non-Canon Weaknesses===
====Ben 10: Omniverse (Graphic Novels)====
If Feedback absorbs an enormous amount of energy to the point of overloading himself, it causes him to explode, revert back to [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] and cause malfunctions on the [[Omnitrix (Omniverse)|Omnitrix]], preventing Ben from transforming again.{{Refn|''[[Ghost Ship]]''|group = OV}}

==History==
===Ben 10===
*Feedback was unlocked off-screen after '''''[[Ben 10: Destroy All Aliens]]'''''.{{Refn|[[:File:OV Spitter Unlocked During Flashbacks.PNG]]|group = DJW}}

===Five Years Prior to Omniverse=== 
*Feedback first appeared in ''[[The More Things Change: Part 1]]'', where he defeated [[Malware]].
*In ''[[A Jolt From the Past]]'', Feedback defeated the [[Nosedeenian|Megawhatts]].
*In ''[[Trouble Helix]]'', Feedback battled Malware.
*In ''[[Of Predators and Prey: Part 2]]'', Feedback fought [[Phil Billings (Classic)|Phil]] as [[Terroranchula (Transformation)|Terroranchula]]. 
**The same scene reoccurred in a flashback in ''[[Max's Monster]]''.
*In ''[[Malefactor]]'', Feedback battled Malware while [[Khyber]] was retrieving a [[Smuggled Psycholeopterran|Psycholeopterran]] DNA sample for the [[Nemetrix]].
*In ''[[Showdown: Part 1]]'', Feedback appeared four times. Firstly, Feedback defeated the [[Violet Offenders]]. Afterwards, Feedback somehow saved some people from a burning building. Later, Feedback practiced with his powers. Lastly, he briefly fought Malware before he was forcibly removed from the Omnitrix and destroyed by the latter.{{Refn|Different crew members have had different interpretations of what happened to Feedback:
*[[Matt Wayne]] believes that Feedback was locked from [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Young Ben's]] [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]].{{Refn|[[:File:Malware locked Feedback.png]]|group = MW}}
*[[Derrick J. Wyatt]] believed that Feedback was removed, with his DNA no longer being present in the [[Codon Stream]] altogether. This evidenced by [[Albedo]] not gaining access to Feedback's DNA when he received the ability to transform into any species.<ref>''[[Double or Nothing]]''</ref>{{Refn|[[:File:Feedback's DNA Not in Alteration Field.PNG]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:Malware Absorbed Feedback's Genetic Fragments.png]]|group = DJW|name = djw feedback}}
*[[Kevin Rubio]] believes that Malware absorbed Feedback and a little bit of Ben's genetic code. However, he stated that [[Matt Youngberg]]'s interpretation would supersede his.{{Refn|[[:File:Kevin Rubio's Explanation on Feedback.png]]|group = KR|name = ben code}}
*Matt Youngberg believes that Malware absorbed Feedback's genetic code, and that [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]] removed [[Conductoid]] DNA from all subsequent Omnitrices.{{Refn|[[:File:Matt Youngberg's Explanation on Feedback 1.png]]|group = MY}}{{Refn|[[:File:Matt Youngberg's Explanation on Feedback 2.png]]|group = MY|name = youngberg feedback}}
|group=note}}

===Omniverse===
*In ''[[Showdown: Part 2]]'', [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] regained access to Feedback after forgiving his younger self{{Refn|Kevin Rubio believes that Ben was able to talk to his younger self because Malware absorbed Feedback and a little bit of Ben's genetic code when he destroyed Feedback. Thus, part of him really was missing.{{Refn|group = KR|name = ben code}} Correlating with this, Matt Youngberg and Derrick J. Wyatt believe that Ben reabsorbed Feedback's DNA when he was floating inside Malware.{{Refn|group = MY|name = youngberg feedback}}{{Refn|group = DJW|name = djw feedback}}|group = note}} and, with help from [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]], destroyed Malware for good.
*In ''[[T.G.I.S.]]'', Feedback defeated [[V.V. Argost|Argost]].
*In ''[[Store 23]]'', Feedback defeated [[Liam]].
*In ''[[Max's Monster]]'', Feedback defeated Phil and reverted him from his [[Terroranchula]] form.
*In ''[[A Fistful of Brains]]'', Feedback defeated [[Albedo|Negative]] [[Ultimate Humungousaur]].
*In ''[[Rad Monster Party]]'', Feedback fought [[Zs'Skayr]].
*In ''[[Weapon XI: Part 1]]'', Feedback defeated Phil and reverted him from his Terroranchula form.
*In ''[[Clyde 5]]'', Feedback located Liam after discovering he was the one who was controlling the [[Cincotrix]] while [[Clyde Fife|Clyde]] was using it.
*In ''[[Breakpoint]]'', Feedback failed to catch [[Fistrick]].
*In ''[[Vreedlemania]]'', Feedback fought the [[Pretty Boy Clones|Pretty Boys]] and watched [[Ma Vreedle]] scare off [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]].
*In ''[[Let's Do the Time War Again]]'', Feedback defeated [[Subdora]] and accidentally stopped time when he battled the [[Time Beast]].
*In ''[[Malgax Attacks]]'', [[Skurd]] gave [[Whampire]] Feedback's arms to fight [[Malware Armor|Mal]][[Vilgax (Classic)|gax]].
*In ''[[The Most Dangerous Game Show]]'', Feedback attempted to battle [[Charles Zenith]] but was immediately reverted by him.
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Feedback absorbed the energy released by [[Maltruant]]'s [[Annihilarrgh]] and defeated him with it, trapping the latter in a time loop for all eternity.

