==Etymology==
[[Wikipedia:Feedback|Feedback]], in electronics, is the process of returning part of the output of a system to the input; this references Feedback's ability to absorb and then redistribute energy.

==Trivia==
*Feedback, [[Grey Matter (Classic)|Grey Matter]], and [[Juryrigg]] are the only aliens with their own theme song. 
**Feedback's theme sounds extremely similar to the song ''[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LwmdNUtreKI You Need to Stop]'' by Osmo Band.
*Feedback and [[Diamondhead (Classic)|Diamondhead]] are the only aliens who have ever defeated [[Malware]]. 
**Due to the loss of Feedback, he is one of the four regular aliens to be temporarily destroyed and removed from the [[Omnitrix (Original)|original Omnitrix]]/[[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]]; the others being [[Chromastone]], [[Way Big (Classic)|Way Big]], and [[Swampfire]].
*Whenever Feedback speaks, an electrical sound is heard.
*Feedback is the first new alien transformation to appear on-screen in '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]'''. He is also the final alien used by 16-year-old Ben on-screen in '''Omniverse''', as well as the Classic Continuity as a whole.
*[[Ben 23]] had originally named [[Feedback (Dimension 23)|his version  of Feedback]] "Plug Man", but eventually changed it due to liking the name "Feedback" better.<ref>''[[Store 23]]''</ref>
*[[Duncan Rouleau]] believes that Feedback is one of few exceptions to the principle that transformations are not full-blown aliens due to retaining Ben's personality, memories, and consciousness; the other example being [[Ghostfreak]].{{Refn|[[:File:Alien DNA Injected.PNG]]|group = DR}}{{Refn|[[:File:Most Aliens Aren't Full Aliens.png]]|group = DR}}
*Due to his DNA being absent from the Codon Stream during ''[[Double or Nothing]]'', Albedo is unable to turn into Feedback.{{Refn|[[:File:Albedo Doesn't Have Feedback.PNG]]|group = DJW}}
**Similarly, [[Mad Ben]] does not have Feedback available in his [[Power Watch|Omnitrix]].{{Refn|[[:File:Mad Ben Does Not Have Feedback.png]]|group = DJW}} However, it is unknown if [[Bad Ben]], [[Benzarro]], or [[Nega Ben]] each have Feedback available in their Omnitricies.{{Refn|[[:File:Mad Ben Feedback.png]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:Alternate Bens Feedback.png]]|group = DJW}}
*[[Derrick J. Wyatt]] once claimed that Feedback's appearance is actually a containment suit,{{Refn|[[:File:Conductoid Containment Suit.png]]|group = DJW}} like [[NRG]], but he eventually refuted the statement, admitting that he was wrong.{{Refn|[[:File:Feedback Not Containment Suit.PNG]]|group = DJW}}
*Feedback was designed by [[Dave Johnson]] at the request of [[Derrick J. Wyatt]] so he could look more like an '''[[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)|Original Series]]''' alien.{{Refn|[[:File:Dave's Feedback Details.png]]|group = DJ}}{{Refn|[[:File:Derrick's Contributions to OV Aliens.png]]|group = DJW}}
**This explains why 11-year-old Feedback's color scheme is similar that of outfits worn by many of 10/11-year-old [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]]'s aliens throughout the Classic Continuity, particularly [[Buzzshock (Classic)|Buzzshock]]'s design in both the '''Original Series''' and '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]'''.
*The concept of Feedback came from [[Glen Murakami]] and [[Dwayne McDuffie]]'s story ideas,{{Refn|[[:File:Glen and Dwayne's Idea For Feedback.PNG]]|group = DJW|name = history}} and had already started by the time Derrick joined the crew.{{Refn|[[:File:Derrick Came Up With Whampire.png]]|group = DJW}}
**Feedback's powers were conceived before Dave came up with his design.{{Refn|[[:File:Feedback's Powers Came Before Design.png]]|group = DJW}}
*The loss of Feedback, who was Ben's favorite alien at the time, was supposed to be the reason Ben took off the original Omnitrix and retired from being a hero,{{Refn|[[:File:Reason For Ben Removing the Omnitrix.png]]|group = MW}}{{Refn|group = DJW|name = history}} but it was ultimately [[Cartoon Network]] executives who vetoed the idea, which many crew members were thankful for.{{Refn|[[:File:CN Vetoed Dwayne and Glen's Feedback Idea.png]]|group = DJW}}
*In ''[[FusionFall Heroes]]'', Feedback has a yellow eye and a pupil, even though he doesn't have either in the show.
*According to [[Yuri Lowenthal]], Feedback has the heroic voice that he always wanted for himself.{{Refn|https://preservetube.com/watch?v&#61;bFHvMBKvoQw|group = YL}}
**Feedback is also one of Yuri's favorite aliens.
*Feedback was considered to appear in the [[Ben 10 (2016 TV Series)|Reboot]] but did not make the cut as an electric alien for [[Ben Tennyson (Reboot)|Ben]] because [[Shock Rock]] was created for plot purposes.{{Refn|[[:File:Shock Rock's Purpose.png]]|group = DR}}
*Feedback is the first mistransformation in '''Omniverse''' that Ben was not upset at.
